{
  "an9.37:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.37 ",
  "an9.37:0.2": "4. The Great Chapter ",
  "an9.37:0.3": "By Ānanda ",
  "an9.37:1.1": "At one time Venerable Ānanda was staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "an9.37:1.2": "There Ānanda addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an9.37:1.3": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an9.37:1.4": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an9.37:1.5": "Ānanda said this: ",
  "an9.37:2.1": "“It’s incredible, reverends, it’s amazing! ",
  "an9.37:2.2": "How this Blessed One who knows and sees, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha, has found an opening amid confinement. It’s in order to purify sentient beings, to get past sorrow and crying, to make an end of pain and sadness, to discover the system, and to realize extinguishment. ",
  "an9.37:2.3": "The eye itself is actually present, and so are those sights. Yet one will not experience that sense-field. ",
  "an9.37:2.4": "The ear itself is actually present, and so are those sounds. Yet one will not experience that sense-field. ",
  "an9.37:2.5": "The nose itself is actually present, and so are those smells. Yet one will not experience that sense-field. ",
  "an9.37:2.6": "The tongue itself is actually present, and so are those tastes. Yet one will not experience that sense-field. ",
  "an9.37:2.7": "The body itself is actually present, and so are those touches. Yet one will not experience that sense-field.” ",
  "an9.37:3.1": "When he said this, Venerable Udāyī said to Venerable Ānanda: ",
  "an9.37